{"title":"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Easiest)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Easiest)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Intuition)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Intuition)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A thin piece of wood of uniform density in the shape of an equilateral triangle with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inches weighs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> ounces. A second piece of the same type of wood, with the same thickness, also in the shape of an equilateral triangle, has side length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inches. Which of the following is closest to the weight, in ounces, of the second piece?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/5/9453b49b0222721f19101ab57b8f5c4e48211ab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 14.0\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 16.0\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 20.0\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 33.3\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 55.6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"464\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Easiest.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Easiest)\">Solution 1 (Easiest)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Easiest)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It is known that \\( Density = \\frac{mass}{volume} \\). You can remember this through \\( D = \\frac{m}{v} \\) (DMV - Like the car lol).\n</p><p>The mass for the triangle with side length 3 is 12 oz. The volume however, we calculate as the area. The only difference that we need to account for is to calculate the area of the other triangle, and not its volume.\n</p><p>The area of the equilateral triangle of length 3 is \\( \\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\). The area of the equilateral triangle of side length 5 is \\( \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\).\n</p><p>Let \\( M \\) be the mass of the triangle of length 5. Our ratio is \\( \\frac{12}{\\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{4}} = \\frac{M}{\\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{4}} \\). Cross multiplying gives us\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b4c983e26d45d9b8ed8bd39d5ba7b1dbd56400d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[12 \\cdot \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{4} = \\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{4} M\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/b/8fb09191c15c8fda1de713240e7f58ff9ea01ba9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Rightarrow 75\\sqrt{3} = \\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{4} M\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/b/8ab91a93bfd4778148d069b58aadcf23c3ea1732.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Rightarrow 300\\sqrt{3} = 9\\sqrt{3}M\\]\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/0/fb0d494b79cb9e0e4abeefcae164b5d89b06dca7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Rightarrow \\frac{300\\sqrt{3}}{9\\sqrt{3}} = M\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bff18d693abebda85730f1a83e2f71432e6c621b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Rightarrow \\frac{300}{9} = M\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>\\( M \\approx \\) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/a/c6a4c9b7a0faebe63a6203986cc144d8c8acabc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 33.3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"79\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p><p><br />\nTs NOT the easiest btw\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can solve this problem by using similar triangles, since two equilateral triangles are always similar. We can then use\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/b/19b722078c8c472d50c3157b477c391ca6d4691e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^2=\\frac{12}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"91\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p><p>We can then solve the equation to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/2/0e24b1191a1a8962b9342ebaa6f3c61ed55a206a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{100}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"64\" height=\"37\" /> which is closest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/a/c6a4c9b7a0faebe63a6203986cc144d8c8acabc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 33.3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"79\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Also recall that the area of an equilateral triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/f/70f352ecf06f8eef197888240835e1e8cf0a04fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a^2\\sqrt3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"43\" height=\"41\" />\nso we can give a ratio as follows:\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a19f0ffc496d97460226111047deb43e06c90007.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{9\\sqrt3}{4}}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"34\" height=\"46\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5eb8726a34932d28103ce7ce17456421222603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/8/d784aab658609ef595dab03c694048d35d5155de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{25\\sqrt3}{4}}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"37\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Cross multiplying and simplifying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/7/e9758d96836a54074f506633b57b2f82a98285a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\cdot \\frac{25}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"52\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/a/6aa67626f8aa81de287cc7eb5ad5d8f8587cc5f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33.\\overline{3}$\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acbc54ef8feabfc5d0a2329f0cfbd10af8a6a809.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\approx$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"11\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/a/c6a4c9b7a0faebe63a6203986cc144d8c8acabc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 33.3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"79\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li>Solution by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/7/3d7a32be44b9cd3f79438aad4c3b5c3f427223eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOPS12142015$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"126\" height=\"13\" /></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the ratio of the two triangle's weights is equal to the ratio of their areas, as the height is the same. The ratio of their areas is equal to the square of the ratio of their sides. So if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> denotes the  weight of the second triangle, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffa8e6a726de50505f6c51db032d2c9aef0d51a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x}{12}=\\frac{5^2}{3^2}=\\frac{25}{9}\\]\" width=\"109\" height=\"39\" /> Solving gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/c/aac84264e7b80bc48a99f417391ba4c16a3aaa1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\approx 33.33$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" /> so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/a/c6a4c9b7a0faebe63a6203986cc144d8c8acabc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 33.3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"79\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Note: In general, the weight would be directly proportional to the volume. However, we are told they have equal height, so we essentially treat the problem as 2D.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Intuition.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Intuition)\">Solution 5 (Intuition)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Intuition)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We ignore the height in this solution because it's constant with both triangles; thus, it has no effect on the difference in their respective weights. Now here's the intuition: notice how the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangle is simply scaled by a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/e/9ae6ca439f90be5b87b92cab8cfd6ea9e3f23475.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> on each length to form the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangle, which means that intuitively on one length the weight is scaled by that factor, and we note that we have 2-dimensional system since we ignored the height; therefore, we proceed by doing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/91717fe5185542df9f4d19155cd44d1c70100185.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{5}{3}\\right)^2 \\cdot 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"80\" height=\"48\" /> to get our desired result as  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/a/c6a4c9b7a0faebe63a6203986cc144d8c8acabc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 33.3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"79\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~triggod\n~edited by someone else\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zUzgzT1kFyo\">https://youtu.be/zUzgzT1kFyo</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/iAE4sL27on4\">https://youtu.be/iAE4sL27on4</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B\">2016 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017015335\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 278/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2322/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 156/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6229/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.866      1 -total\n 60.35%    7.765      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 38.62%    4.969      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14786:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017015335 and revision id 290555. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}